<threat_model>
## Trust Boundaries

| Boundary | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| client → GET /api/compliance/score | JWT-authenticated; tenant_id extracted from verified token, never from request body or query param |
| backend → MongoDB compliance_frameworks | Global collection, no tenant injection — correct; frameworks are platform-wide reference data |
| backend → MongoDB asset_compliance | TenantIsolatedCollection auto-injects tenantId from request context — prevents cross-tenant reads |
| backend → Redis/fakeredis | Cache key includes tenant_id from JWT; super admin uses separate key |

## STRIDE Threat Register

| Threat ID | Category | Component | Disposition | Mitigation Plan |
|-----------|----------|-----------|-------------|-----------------|
| T-09-01 | Information Disclosure | cache key in get_compliance_score | mitigate | Cache key = "compliance:score:{tenant_id}" from JWT; super admin key is "compliance:score:__super__" — no cross-tenant cache collision |
| T-09-02 | Tampering | cache_key derivation | mitigate | tenant_id from JWT (get_current_user dependency), not from user-supplied input; key is not user-controllable |
| T-09-03 | Denial of Service | repeated GET /api/compliance/score cache-busting | accept | TTL=300s limits recomputation to once per 5 min per tenant; rate_limiter.py is already applied globally |
| T-09-04 | Spoofing | unauthenticated access to score endpoint | mitigate | get_current_user dependency raises 401 on missing/invalid JWT; consistent with all other compliance endpoints |
| T-09-05 | Information Disclosure | asset_compliance raw motor bypass | mitigate | Score endpoint uses db.asset_compliance (TenantIsolatedCollection) not db._db.asset_compliance; reviewed in Task 2 action |
| T-09-SC | Tampering | npm/pip installs | accept | No new packages in this plan; all implementation uses existing project dependencies (no install tasks) |
</threat_model>

